摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Kimi Code written in DSH form: the kimi-cli tool surface re-registered as native DeepSeek Harness tools.","id":"gh:1333497662","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-kernel-kimi","slug":"oppnc/dsh-kernel-kimi","topics":["coding-agent","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","kimi","kimi-cli","moonshot"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Kimi Code written in DSH form: the kimi-cli tool surface re-registered as native DeepSeek Harness to"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" Code written in DSH form: the kimi-cli tool surface re-registered as native DeepSeek Harness tools."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"# dsh-kernel-kimi"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"DSH runs on one simple idea: **everything is a plugin**. Models, tools, subagents — plug them togeth"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"er however you like."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"So we did exactly that: we turned **Kimi Code into a DSH plugin**. The Kimi Code CLI 0.39.1 tool sur"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"face you already know — `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Glob`, `Grep`, `Bash`, `ReadMediaFile`, `WebSearch"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"`, `FetchURL`, `TaskList`, `TaskOutput`, `TaskStop`, `WaitFor`, `TodoList`, `AskUserQuestion`, `Skil"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"l`, `Agent`, `AgentSwarm`, `CreateGoal`, `GetGoal`, `SetGoalBudget`, `UpdateGoal`, `CronCreate`, `Cr"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"onList`, `CronDelete`, `ExitPlanMode`, `EnterPlanMode` — is now a set of native DSH tools. Same name"},{"id":"p5s6","text":"s, same schemas, same behavior."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The payoff is simple: use the kimi CLI natively inside DSH — **no different** from opening Kimi Code"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" itself. Every model stays in the environment it knows best — main agent or subagent, it feels like "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"ry model stays in the environment it knows best — main agent or subagent, it feels like coming home."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"`WebSearch` / `FetchURL` talk to the same Moonshot endpoints the Kimi CLI uses (`api.kimi.com/coding"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"/v1/search` and `/fetch`) with the shared OAuth token. Distilled from Kimi Code CLI **0.39.1** (`@mo"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"onshot-ai/kimi-code`)."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> We differentially verified against the real kimi CLI: the same task on the same directory produces"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" identical results, item by item."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## System prompt & subagents"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"`lib/system-prompt.js` carries the upstream **Kimi Code CLI** `system.md` (runtime\nplaceholders adap"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ted to DSH); `apply()` registers it as the agent's sole\nsystem-prompt section (`complete: true` + `s"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"uppressRuntimeContext()`)."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"`lib/subagents.js` ships the kernel's own subagent recipes — `kimi-agent`\n(coder), `kimi-explore`, `"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"kimi-plan` — each = the full system prompt with the\nupstream `roleAdditional` block inserted. The me"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"sh loads them and mounts this\nplugin on each child with a `config.tools` whitelist."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"1. Install the plugin into your profile with the official plugin command:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"GitHub also works (`dsh plugin --profile web add github:oppnc/dsh-kernel-kimi`) because `lib/` ships"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"`dsh plugin --profile web add github:oppnc/dsh-kernel-kimi`) because `lib/` ships in the repository."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"This package is a plain plugin (no `dsh.bundle` declaration), so `dsh plugin` installs it as an inac"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"tive dependency — that is expected: the preset row below references it by name."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"2. The `kimi-kernel` agent preset ships in `dsh-kernel-mesh`'s `presets/` directory. Copy it into th"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"e official user-preset root (or, if you run without the mesh, get the preset directory from the mesh"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ial user-preset root (or, if you run without the mesh, get the preset directory from the mesh repo):"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"The preset already includes the `kimi-surface` row inside the **planning** group (so the plan tools "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"can reach `planMode`); if you author your own preset, add it there:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Start a session on the `kimi-kernel` preset and pick the model `kimi-kernel/k3-256k`. Your main agen"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"t runs on the Kimi kernel with the full kimi tool surface."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"MIT — see LICENSE."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
